{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr4NH4N9U4Jcstg8tCJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open any files, so this diagnosis comes from how this NestJS boilerplate normally works. I haven't confirmed it against your code, and the line ranges are estimates.\n\nLogin rejects any user whose `provider` isn't `AuthProvidersEnum.email`. It builds the 422 message `needLoginViaProvider:${user.provider}` from the stored value. A message ending in `google` means the new user was saved with `provider = 'google'`. The most likely place for that is `UsersService.create`, which should default `provider` to `email`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"248f7101-d238-4c28-be87-b295a44d7b5d","uuid":"865ee6fa-5edf-43bc-9408-e2747a799893","timestamp":"2026-11-08T20:03:15.725Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr4NGswzj3kRWx8hJGZt"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr4NH4N9U4Jcstg8tCJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015ZRr4a2Q84uQQ9cVcxXqGv","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","symbol":"UsersService.create","start_line":30,"end_line":120,"explanation":"On user creation the provider should default to AuthProvidersEnum.email (`createUserDto.provider ?? AuthProvidersEnum.email`). A wrong default here, such as AuthProvidersEnum.google, would store every email-registered user with provider 'google'. Login would then reject them with needLoginViaProvider:google. This is the most likely cause."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.register","start_line":150,"end_line":190,"explanation":"Register calls usersService.create without a provider and relies on the default. If it passes or spreads a wrong provider value, the user is stored as google. Login in the same file then rejects them in validateLogin, where the provider check lives."},{"file":"src/users/infrastructure/persistence/relational/entities/user.entity.ts","symbol":"UserEntity.provider","start_line":40,"end_line":50,"explanation":"The provider column default, and the equivalent in the document schema, may be set to google or otherwise wrong. If so, a user saved without an explicit provider would get that value."}],"fix":{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","description":"In UsersService.create, set provider to `createUserDto.provider ?? AuthProvidersEnum.email`. Make sure AuthService.register does not pass a provider. Also check that the provider column default in the user entity and document schema is 'email'."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"out